# LF in the repository, always. `* -text` switched normalisation off, so a Windows
# checkout could commit CRLF and turn every touched file into a whole-file diff.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary

# ⛔ Keep dev files out of `git archive`, which is how deploy-export.cmd builds the
# FTP-ready folder. Without these, .gitignore and .gitattributes ship to the client's
# server — harmless but untidy, and preflight blocks the export for it.
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.gitignore    export-ignore
/bin           export-ignore

# Same rule, for the test and CI tooling. None of it is runtime code: shipping a tests/
# directory and a CI workflow to a client's wp-content/plugins is noise at best, and at
# worst it advertises the toolchain to anyone who can read the folder.
/.github       export-ignore
/tests         export-ignore
/phpcs.xml     export-ignore
/phpunit.xml   export-ignore
/.wp-env.json  export-ignore

# 2026-09-19: composer.json only feeds Composer tooling; the plugin loads through its own PSR-4 fallback autoloader.
/composer.json export-ignore
